      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "We only evaluate on validation set. Initially, we combined train+TTT into one stage for convenience (only validation \"train\" examples in training, \"test\" excluded), but that shouldn't cause additional leakage compared to the two-staged train -> TTT (validation \"train\" examples are also included in second stage. Otherwise accuracy would be 100% with appropriate hyperparameter configuration, but we had never found across sweeps and Transformer baselines). \n\nBesides, thanks for the proposal! We're splitting the two stages, as \"annealing\" on the higher quality TTT-stage may improve performance. We welcome help and PR on this approach.",
