  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "Hi, first I wanted to say awesome work on the Hierarchical Reasoning Model, super interesting approach, seems especially promising on the Sudoku and Mazes approach.\n\nHowever, I believe I spotted a data leak in the training and evaluation process for the ARC-AGI dataset. It looks like the model is trained on all of the training dataset and validation dataset example pairs & test pairs, which inflates the metrics unfairly.\n\nI suggest you might want to still train on 300/400 of the validation examples and reserve the 100 others for a completely blind final tests. Test-time training (TTT) could use those reserved 100 example pairs, but never for their test outputs.\n\nThe approach seems super promising so it would be great you see how it performs with a distinct train/validation split! Let me know if I can help with a PR or more details - happy to chat!",
  "closed_at": "2025-08-04T06:27:00Z",
